    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d519">

                <pb facs="0683" n="609" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg609"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/6101</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the British Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Spring Rice</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-08-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 1, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir
                            Cecil</hi>: Referring to the paraphrase of a telegram from
                    London which you left with Mr. Phillips on
                    Saturday afternoon, July 28, regarding a conference of shipping representatives
                    of Allied countries soon to be held in London in order to discuss the whole
                    shipping problem, I beg to say that it has been decided that inasmuch as there
                    is a conference on shipping being held here now it would be well for this
                    Government to await the result of this conference before taking part in the
                    conference suggested in London.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank L. Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
